{
  "model": "google/gemini-3-8-flash-lite-tts",
  "openapi": {
    "openapi": "3.1.0",
    "info": {
      "title": "kie.ai",
      "description": "kie.ai API 文档",
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "contact": {
        "name": "技术支持",
        "email": "support@kie.ai"
      }
    },
    "tags": [],
    "paths": {
      "/api/v1/jobs/createTask": {
        "post": {
          "summary": "Gemini 3.8 Flash Lite Text to speech",
          "deprecated": false,
          "description": "Text-to-speech with Gemini 3.8 Flash Lite.\n\nOutput: WAV (16-bit PCM, 24 kHz, mono).\n\n## Query Task Status\n\nAfter submitting a task, use the unified query endpoint to check progress and retrieve results:\n\n<Card title=\"Get Task Details\" icon=\"lucide-search\" href=\"/market/common/get-task-detail\">\n  Learn how to query task status and retrieve generation results\n</Card>\n\n::: tip[]\nFor production use, we recommend using the `callBackUrl` parameter to receive automatic notifications when generation completes, rather than polling the status endpoint.\n:::\n\n## Related Resources\n\n<CardGroup cols={3}>\n  <Card title=\"Market Overview\" icon=\"lucide-store\" href=\"/market/quickstart\">\n    Explore all available models\n  </Card>\n  <Card title=\"File Upload API\" icon=\"lucide-cog\" href=\"/file-upload-api/quickstart\">\n    Learn how to upload and manage files\n  </Card>\n  <Card title=\"Common API\" icon=\"lucide-webhook\" href=\"/common-api/get-account-credits\">\n    Check credits and account usage\n  </Card>\n</CardGroup>",
          "operationId": "gemini-3-8-flash-lite-tts",
          "tags": [],
          "parameters": [],
          "requestBody": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "model": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "description": "Model to be used",
                      "enum": [
                        "google/gemini-3-8-flash-lite-tts"
                      ],
                      "default": "google/gemini-3-8-flash-lite-tts"
                    },
                    "callBackUrl": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "description": "Callback URL for the result"
                    },
                    "input": {
                      "type": "object",
                      "description": "Input parameters for the generation task",
                      "properties": {
                        "temperature": {
                          "type": "number",
                          "minimum": 0,
                          "maximum": 2,
                          "default": 1,
                          "description": "Sampling temperature, e.g., 1"
                        },
                        "speakers": {
                          "type": "array",
                          "description": "List of speaker configurations. Each speaker uses either `voice_name` (preset voice) or `replica` (voice clone); the two are mutually exclusive. If neither is sent, the speaker defaults to `Fola`.",
                          "items": {
                            "type": "object",
                            "properties": {
                              "speaker_id": {
                                "type": "string",
                                "description": "Speaker identifier, e.g., \"Speaker 1\" or \"Speaker 2\". Must be in \"Speaker N\" format."
                              },
                              "voice_name": {
                                "type": "string",
                                "description": "Voice name. Mutually exclusive with `replica`: send only one of `voice_name` or `replica` for the same speaker. Omit this field when using voice cloning. If neither this field nor `replica` is sent, default is `Fola`.\n\n70 voices grouped by use case:\n\n- Tutor: Bodi, Lumi, Sadaltager, Sola, Sulafat, Varo, Zephyr\n- Commercial Voiceover: Koda, Kore, Nika, Tavi, Zeno\n- Instructional: Algenib, Despina, Erinome, Kira, Ludo, Mako, Rasalgethi, Rina\n- Podcast: Alnilam, Brio, Jori, Laomedeia, Rami, Veda\n- Storyteller: Achird, Enzo, Riko, Sami, Zali, Zubenelgenubi\n- Digital Assistant: Algieba, Aoede, Autonoe, Callirrhoe, Enceladus, Gero, Iapetus, Neno, Olin, Tari, Umbriel\n- Call Center: Achernar, Charon, Daro, Fola, Hali, Milo, Puck\n- Concierge: Arlo, Cleo, Fenrir, Finn, Leda, Lora, Orus\n- Tech Support: Enya, Jett, Knox, Nyla, Sadachbia, Vindemiatrix\n- Professional: Cruz, Elio, Gacrux, Pulcherrima, Schedar, Tova, Zuri",
                                "enum": [
                                  "Bodi",
                                  "Lumi",
                                  "Sadaltager",
                                  "Sola",
                                  "Sulafat",
                                  "Varo",
                                  "Zephyr",
                                  "Koda",
                                  "Kore",
                                  "Nika",
                                  "Tavi",
                                  "Zeno",
                                  "Algenib",
                                  "Despina",
                                  "Erinome",
                                  "Kira",
                                  "Ludo",
                                  "Mako",
                                  "Rasalgethi",
                                  "Rina",
                                  "Alnilam",
                                  "Brio",
                                  "Jori",
                                  "Laomedeia",
                                  "Rami",
                                  "Veda",
                                  "Achird",
                                  "Enzo",
                                  "Riko",
                                  "Sami",
                                  "Zali",
                                  "Zubenelgenubi",
                                  "Algieba",
                                  "Aoede",
                                  "Autonoe",
                                  "Callirrhoe",
                                  "Enceladus",
                                  "Gero",
                                  "Iapetus",
                                  "Neno",
                                  "Olin",
                                  "Tari",
                                  "Umbriel",
                                  "Achernar",
                                  "Charon",
                                  "Daro",
                                  "Fola",
                                  "Hali",
                                  "Milo",
                                  "Puck",
                                  "Arlo",
                                  "Cleo",
                                  "Fenrir",
                                  "Finn",
                                  "Leda",
                                  "Lora",
                                  "Orus",
                                  "Enya",
                                  "Jett",
                                  "Knox",
                                  "Nyla",
                                  "Sadachbia",
                                  "Vindemiatrix",
                                  "Cruz",
                                  "Elio",
                                  "Gacrux",
                                  "Pulcherrima",
                                  "Schedar",
                                  "Tova",
                                  "Zuri"
                                ],
                                "default": "Fola"
                              },
                              "replica": {
                                "type": "object",
                                "title": "TTSVoiceReplica",
                                "description": "Voice clone settings. Gemini 3.8 only. Optional. Mutually exclusive with `voice_name` — do not send both on the same speaker.\n\nWhen set, this task temporarily clones the speaker from two recordings. The clone is not saved as a reusable voice. You can pass `replica` for a speaker in both single-speaker and two-speaker requests.\n\nBoth recordings must be of the same adult, captured with the same microphone in the same room. AI-generated audio is rejected.\n\nWAV only. Recommended: 24kHz, mono, 16-bit PCM. Max 10MB per file. Format is detected from file content, not the extension or Content-Type.",
                                "properties": {
                                  "source_audio_url": {
                                    "type": "string",
                                    "format": "uri",
                                    "description": "URL of the reference recording. The file must be directly downloadable. Record 10–30 seconds of natural speech in a quiet space: no echo, no background music, and only one voice. Record in the language you will generate."
                                  },
                                  "consent_audio_url": {
                                    "type": "string",
                                    "format": "uri",
                                    "description": "URL of the consent recording. The file must be directly downloadable. The same person as in the reference recording must read this sentence verbatim:\n\nI am the owner of this voice and I consent to Google using this voice to create a synthetic voice model.\n\nOther supported language versions of this sentence are also accepted. Trim silence and noise at the start and end."
                                  }
                                },
                                "required": [
                                  "source_audio_url",
                                  "consent_audio_url"
                                ]
                              }
                            },
                            "required": [
                              "speaker_id"
                            ],
                            "not": {
                              "required": [
                                "voice_name",
                                "replica"
                              ]
                            }
                          }
                        },
                        "filler_words": {
                          "type": "boolean",
                          "default": false,
                          "description": "Whether to insert filler words in two-speaker dialogue. Off by default (omit this field); when enabled, the request includes `\"filler_words\": true`. Only takes effect when `speakers` has two speakers (e.g. Speaker 1 and Speaker 2). When two people are speaking, you can turn on this switch."
                        },
                        "dialogue_turns": {
                          "type": "array",
                          "description": "List of dialogue turns, output in sequential order",
                          "items": {
                            "type": "object",
                            "properties": {
                              "speaker_id": {
                                "type": "string",
                                "description": "Corresponding speaker identifier, e.g., \"Speaker 1\""
                              },
                              "text": {
                                "type": "string",
                                "description": "The speaker's line. May include tone tags wrapped in English angle brackets. Example: Hello there. `<laugh>` That works.\n\nOfficial insertable tags: `<argh>`, `<breath>`, `<cackle>`, `<cheer>`, `<chuckle>`, `<chuckles>`, `<cough>`, `<cry>`, `<exhales>`, `<gasp>`, `<giggle>`, `<groan>`, `<growl>`, `<grr>`, `<grunt>`, `<heavy breath>`, `<hiss>`, `<laugh>`, `<laughter>`, `<long pause>`, `<moan>`, `<pant>`, `<pff>`, `<phew>`, `<scream>`, `<short pause>`, `<shout>`, `<shriek>`, `<sigh>`, `<sighs>`, `<sneeze>`, `<snicker>`, `<snort>`, `<sob>`, `<throat-clearing>`, `<tsk>`, `<whimper>`, `<whispering>`, `<whispers>`, `<yawn>`.",
                                "maxLength": 10000,
                                "examples": [
                                  "Hello there. <laugh> That works."
                                ]
                              },
                              "style": {
                                "type": "string",
                                "description": "Per-turn speaking style, 3.8 only. Freely describe tone, emotion, and pace; different lines from the same speaker can differ. Example: Speak like a tired night-shift radio host, slow and dry."
                              }
                            },
                            "required": [
                              "speaker_id",
                              "text"
                            ]
                          }
                        }
                      },
                      "required": [
                        "speakers",
                        "dialogue_turns"
                      ]
                    }
                  },
                  "required": [
                    "model",
                    "input"
                  ]
                },
                "example": {
                  "model": "google/gemini-3-8-flash-lite-tts",
                  "callBackUrl": "https://your-domain.com/api/callback",
                  "input": {
                    "temperature": 1,
                    "speakers": [
                      {
                        "speaker_id": "Speaker 1",
                        "voice_name": "Fola"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker_id": "Speaker 2",
                        "voice_name": "Zephyr"
                      }
                    ],
                    "dialogue_turns": [
                      {
                        "speaker_id": "Speaker 1",
                        "style": "Speak like a tired night-shift radio host, slow and dry.",
                        "text": "Hello there. <laugh> That works."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker_id": "Speaker 2",
                        "style": "Bright and curious, slightly faster.",
                        "text": "Wait, did you hear that? <gasp> I think it actually worked."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                }
              }
            },
            "required": true
          },
          "responses": {
            "200": {
              "description": "Request successful",
              "content": {
                "application/json": {
                  "schema": {
                    "allOf": [
                      {
                        "type": "object",
                        "properties": {
                          "code": {
                            "type": "integer",
                            "enum": [
                              200,
                              401,
                              402,
                              404,
                              422,
                              429,
                              455,
                              500,
                              501,
                              505
                            ],
                            "description": "Status code of the request. The HTTP status is 200 even when the request fails, so always check this field: 200 means success; any other value means the request failed and msg describes the reason. Common values: 401 invalid or missing API key; 402 insufficient credits; 429 rate limit exceeded; 422 or 500 the request could not be processed (read msg and check your parameters before retrying)."
                          },
                          "msg": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Response message, error description when failed",
                            "examples": [
                              "success"
                            ]
                          },
                          "data": {
                            "type": "object",
                            "properties": {
                              "taskId": {
                                "type": "string",
                                "description": "Task ID, can be used with Get Task Details endpoint to query task status"
                              }
                            }
                          }
                        },
                        "required": [
                          "data"
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "example": {
                    "code": 200,
                    "msg": "success",
                    "data": {
                      "taskId": "task_1765185282276"
                    }
                  }
                }
              },
              "headers": {}
            }
          },
          "security": [
            {
              "BearerAuth": []
            }
          ],
          "callbacks": {
            "musicTaskCompleted": {
              "{request.body#/callBackUrl}": {
                "post": {
                  "description": "The system sends this callback when the audio task succeeds or fails.",
                  "requestBody": {
                    "required": true,
                    "content": {
                      "application/json": {
                        "schema": {
                          "type": "object",
                          "required": [
                            "code",
                            "msg",
                            "data"
                          ],
                          "properties": {
                            "code": {
                              "type": "integer",
                              "description": "Unified callback code: 200 for success, 501 for failure.",
                              "enum": [
                                200,
                                501
                              ]
                            },
                            "msg": {
                              "type": "string",
                              "description": "Unified callback message.",
                              "enum": [
                                "Playground task completed successfully.",
                                "Playground task failed."
                              ]
                            },
                            "data": {
                              "type": "object",
                              "required": [
                                "taskId",
                                "model",
                                "state",
                                "param"
                              ],
                              "properties": {
                                "taskId": {
                                  "type": "string",
                                  "description": "The unique task identifier."
                                },
                                "model": {
                                  "type": "string",
                                  "description": "The model used for the task.",
                                  "enum": [
                                    "google/gemini-3-8-flash-lite-tts"
                                  ]
                                },
                                "state": {
                                  "type": "string",
                                  "description": "Terminal task state.",
                                  "enum": [
                                    "success",
                                    "fail"
                                  ]
                                },
                                "param": {
                                  "type": "string",
                                  "description": "JSON string containing the submitted task parameters."
                                },
                                "resultJson": {
                                  "type": "string",
                                  "nullable": true,
                                  "description": "JSON string containing resultUrls and resultObject when successful. Present only when state is success."
                                },
                                "failCode": {
                                  "type": "string",
                                  "nullable": true,
                                  "description": "Failure code, a numeric string such as \"400\" or \"500\". Present only when state is fail."
                                },
                                "failMsg": {
                                  "type": "string",
                                  "nullable": true,
                                  "description": "Failure reason. Present only when state is fail."
                                },
                                "costTime": {
                                  "type": "integer",
                                  "format": "int64",
                                  "description": "Processing time in seconds. Present on both success and failure callbacks."
                                },
                                "completeTime": {
                                  "type": "integer",
                                  "format": "int64",
                                  "description": "Task completion timestamp."
                                },
                                "createTime": {
                                  "type": "integer",
                                  "format": "int64",
                                  "description": "Task creation timestamp."
                                },
                                "updateTime": {
                                  "type": "integer",
                                  "format": "int64",
                                  "description": "Use completeTime as the completion time; updateTime may equal createTime."
                                },
                                "creditsConsumed": {
                                  "type": "number",
                                  "description": "Credits consumed by the task; 0 for failed tasks."
                                }
                              }
                            }
                          }
                        },
                        "examples": {
                          "success": {
                            "summary": "Task completed successfully",
                            "value": {
                              "code": 200,
                              "msg": "Playground task completed successfully.",
                              "data": {
                                "taskId": "task_example_music_webhook_001",
                                "model": "google/gemini-3-8-flash-lite-tts",
                                "state": "success",
                                "param": "{\"input\":\"{\\\"temperature\\\":1,\\\"speakers\\\":[{\\\"speaker_id\\\":\\\"Speaker 1\\\",\\\"voice_name\\\":\\\"Fola\\\"},{\\\"speaker_id\\\":\\\"Speaker 2\\\",\\\"voice_name\\\":\\\"Zephyr\\\"}],\\\"dialogue_turns\\\":[{\\\"speaker_id\\\":\\\"Speaker 1\\\",\\\"style\\\":\\\"Speak like a tired night-shift radio host, slow and dry.\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Hello there. <laugh> That works.\\\"},{\\\"speaker_id\\\":\\\"Speaker 2\\\",\\\"style\\\":\\\"Bright and curious, slightly faster.\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Wait, did you hear that? <gasp> I think it actually worked.\\\"}]}\",\"callBackUrl\":\"https://your-domain.com/api/callback\",\"model\":\"google/gemini-3-8-flash-lite-tts\"}",
                                "resultJson": "{\"resultUrls\":[\"https://example.com/generated-audio.wav\"],\"resultObject\":null}",
                                "costTime": 12,
                                "completeTime": 1234567890,
                                "createTime": 1234560000,
                                "updateTime": 1234567890,
                                "creditsConsumed": 1.23
                              }
                            }
                          },
                          "failure": {
                            "summary": "Task failed",
                            "value": {
                              "code": 501,
                              "msg": "Playground task failed.",
                              "data": {
                                "taskId": "task_example_music_webhook_001",
                                "model": "google/gemini-3-8-flash-lite-tts",
                                "state": "fail",
                                "param": "{\"input\":\"{\\\"temperature\\\":1,\\\"speakers\\\":[{\\\"speaker_id\\\":\\\"Speaker 1\\\",\\\"voice_name\\\":\\\"Fola\\\"},{\\\"speaker_id\\\":\\\"Speaker 2\\\",\\\"voice_name\\\":\\\"Zephyr\\\"}],\\\"dialogue_turns\\\":[{\\\"speaker_id\\\":\\\"Speaker 1\\\",\\\"style\\\":\\\"Speak like a tired night-shift radio host, slow and dry.\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Hello there. <laugh> That works.\\\"},{\\\"speaker_id\\\":\\\"Speaker 2\\\",\\\"style\\\":\\\"Bright and curious, slightly faster.\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Wait, did you hear that? <gasp> I think it actually worked.\\\"}]}\",\"callBackUrl\":\"https://your-domain.com/api/callback\",\"model\":\"google/gemini-3-8-flash-lite-tts\"}",
                                "failCode": "400",
                                "failMsg": "<error detail>",
                                "costTime": 12,
                                "creditsConsumed": 0
                              }
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  "responses": {
                    "200": {
                      "description": "Callback received successfully.",
                      "content": {
                        "application/json": {
                          "schema": {
                            "type": "object",
                            "properties": {
                              "code": {
                                "type": "integer",
                                "example": 200
                              },
                              "msg": {
                                "type": "string",
                                "example": "success"
                              }
                            }
                          },
                          "example": {
                            "code": 200,
                            "msg": "success"
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "webhooks": {},
    "components": {
      "schemas": {
        "ApiResponseWithRecordId": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "code": {
              "type": "integer",
              "enum": [
                200,
                401,
                402,
                404,
                422,
                429,
                455,
                500,
                501,
                505
              ],
              "description": "Status code of the request. The HTTP status is 200 even when the request fails, so always check this field: 200 means success; any other value means the request failed and msg describes the reason. Common values: 401 invalid or missing API key; 402 insufficient credits; 429 rate limit exceeded; 422 or 500 the request could not be processed (read msg and check your parameters before retrying)."
            },
            "msg": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Response message, error description when failed",
              "examples": [
                "success"
              ]
            },
            "data": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "taskId": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "description": "Task ID, can be used with Get Task Details endpoint to query task status"
                },
                "recordId": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "description": "Record ID, can be used to get the record details"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "title": "response with recordId",
          "required": [
            "data"
          ]
        }
      },
      "responses": {},
      "securitySchemes": {
        "BearerAuth": {
          "type": "http",
          "scheme": "bearer",
          "bearerFormat": "API Key",
          "description": "All API requests require a Bearer Token. Add the header `Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY` to authenticate requests."
        }
      }
    },
    "servers": [
      {
        "url": "https://api.kie.ai",
        "description": "正式环境"
      }
    ],
    "security": [
      {
        "BearerAuth": []
      }
    ]
  }
}
